In triangle \( ABC \) with \( \angle B = 90^\circ \), \( AB = 8 \), and \( BC = 3 \), points \( P, Q, R \) are on sides \( BC, CA, AB \) respectively, such that \( \angle CRP = \angle CRQ \) and \( \angle BPR = \angle CPQ \). The perimeter of triangle \( PQR \) is 12. Find the length of the perpendicular from \( Q \) to side \( BC \).<|im_end|>
